cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "rulewarden: Deterministic Runtime Assurance for AI Coding Agents"
message: "If you use this tool, its rule packs, corpus or benchmark, please cite it."
type: software
license: Apache-2.0
version: 0.1.1
date-released: "2026-10-14"
repository-code: "https://github.com/thanatchon36/rulewarden"
url: "https://thanatchon36.github.io/rulewarden/"
authors:
  - family-names: Chongmankhong
    given-names: Thanatchon
abstract: >-
  An open-source, deterministic, fail-closed enforcer for the rules developers write in agent
  instruction files such as CLAUDE.md and AGENTS.md. It maps twelve concepts from safety-critical
  engineering (Simplex, independence of verification, MISRA decidability classes, tool
  qualification, alarm management and others) onto requirements for a rule enforcer, and checks
  each agent change in a pre-tool hook, a git hook and CI. The repository also contains a corpus
  study of 300 public instruction files, which measures how many of their rules are decidable on a
  diff, and a pre-registered benchmark of headless Claude Code runs on 20 tasks under five
  conditions, released with every recording and a key-free replay script.
keywords:
  - ai-coding-agents
  - runtime-assurance
  - claude-code
  - agents-md
  - policy-enforcement
  - safety-critical-systems
  - hooks
